  "name": "Legendary Collection booster box",
  "category": "product_promotion",
  "description": {
    "text": "Legendary Collection, Wizards of the Coast's May 2002 set of reprints of the game's earliest cards, introduced box toppers to the Pokémon TCG: four oversized cards found only in sealed booster boxes, numbered S1/S4 to S4/S4 with a P. Each is a larger reverse holo copy of one of the set's cards, Charizard, Dark Blastoise, Dark Raichu or Mewtwo, with an almost checkered take on the firework pattern of the set's reverse holos. Mitsuhiro Arita drew the first three, Christopher Rush Mewtwo.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Flipside Gaming: Retrospective, Legendary Collection (2018)",
        "url": "https://flipsidegaming.com/blogs/pokemon-blog/retrospective-legendary-collection"
      },
      {
        "title": "Elite Fourum: Jumbo Card Checklist #2",
        "url": "https://www.elitefourum.com/t/jumbo-card-checklist-2/14837"
      }
    ]
  },
